{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>For.</b> Its waters are full of blood; the slain of Moab." "<b>Additions.</b> The meaning is additional evils, as in 'a rich man answers insolence' (Proverbs 18:23); the meaning is words." "<b>For I will bring.</b> He draws also after, likewise 'I will bring upon the fugitives of Moab a lion,' and he is the king of Assyria."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:56.319965127Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}